    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe search highlight covers the multicursors, so they are hidden behind it.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nOpen any text, start search by pressing * on a word. The word is highlighted.\nThen add a multicursor in the middle of that word and move the main cursor on another position.\nThe multicursor is hidden as if the search highlight has more priority.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAs the main cursor is visibile over any search-highlighted word, also the multicursors should be visible in their original hl setting.\n\nIn my opinion this is a problem because:\n- the aestetic behavior of main cursor is different from the multicursors\n- the user is confused because on the screen there isn't evidence of the presence of any multicursors (they are completely hidden)\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1644+gaed60b8a53\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot applicable\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nwsl\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nwez\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nunrelated\n\n### Installation\n\nfrom repo",
